.TH WACKGET 1 "October 2026" "WackGet 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wackget \- download manager: paste or drop links and let it fetch them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wackget
[\fB\-\-toggle\fR]
[\fB\-\-config=\fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-skin=\fINAME\fR]
[\fIURL\fR|\fIQUEUE.wgq\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
WackGet keeps a queue of downloads and fetches a few at a time, resuming partial files and
retrying broken connections. Add links by pasting (Ctrl+V), dragging them onto the window,
opening a .wgq queue file, or naming them on the command line.
.PP
Only one WackGet runs per user: starting it again hands the URLs and queue files to the one
that is already running, or brings its window to the front.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Show the running WackGet, or hide it if it is the window in front. Meant for a keyboard shortcut
made in the desktop's settings.
.TP
.BI \-\-config= FILE
Use \fIFILE\fR for the settings instead of
.IR ~/.config/wackget/wackget.ini .
.TP
.BI \-\-skin= NAME
Start with the \fBclassic\fR, \fBwin11\fR or \fBmaterial1\fR look (not saved).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wackget/
Settings and the download log. The proxy password is kept in the desktop's keyring.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wget (1),
.BR curl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/levoniust/WackGet
